            "review_title": "Review at Popeyes - Maximark Cong Hoa",
            "review_text": "SW_Buddy\n79 contributions\n0\nOMG! The best fried chicken and sides EVER!\nOct 2015 • Friends\nI know I'm not supposed to like fried chicken and other food items dripping animal fat. It'll be the death of me, I KNOW!!! But, please, let me die a happy man. \n\nI don't often have the hankering for fried chicken, but when I do, nothing can satisfy like Popeye's. Nothing. (KFC, you might as well close all of your stores.) And, mind you, I cannot stomach more than one or two pieces of the tasty, crunchy, spicy, and juicy fare. It's too rich. Oh, but what happiness could be had in those few tasty morsels! Just don't mind me when I pick the last crumbs from the basket. \n\nThe side dishes are a different story. Biscuits? OMG! They are flaky, light, and divine...at home in the US. Here in HCMC, they are a bit odd...sweet and dense. How unfortunate. But, the mashed potatoes, dirty rice, and corn are always good accompaniments to the chicken. Now let me be. I feel a hankering coming on...\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten October 7, 2015",
